                  "speaker": "Speaker 2"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2840528,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Personally, I prefer mushrooms cooked, but it won't do you any harm to eat them uncooked in salads.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 154.45001,
                  "from": 146.45,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 2"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2840547,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "It's not necessary to peel them.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 156.93001,
                  "from": 155.01,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 2"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2840554,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "Another thing you should remember is that you can't tell if a mushroom is safe to eat by its smell. Some of the most deadly mushrooms have no smell and taste quite nice, apparently. Finally, just because deer or squirrels eat a particular mushroom doesn't mean that you can.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2840555,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Another thing you should remember is that you can't tell if a mushroom is safe to eat by its smell.",
                "meta": {
